;; The locked profile, as a pack, because locking a systemd console takes
;; files and only packs carry files.
;;
;; BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY=n turns off Buildroot's getty and nothing else.
;; With it off, Buildroot's systemd package leaves upstream systemd's defaults
;; alone (package/systemd/systemd.mk:744), and those start a getty on tty1 by
;; preset and on the kernel's console= by systemd-getty-generator. There is
;; no Kconfig symbol for either. A boot of qemu-arm-agent showed the result:
;; a locked image offering "buildroot login:" that could only fail.
;;
;; The fix was three symlinks to /dev/null, and it lived in the
;; wireguard-appliance pack, so the one image composing that pack was locked
;; and every other locked image was not. It lives here now, with the profile
;; whose claim it makes true.

(capabilities
  (capability no-console-login
    (doc "Nothing offers a login on any console: no getty on a tty, a serial line or /dev/console.")))

(pack locked
  (version "0.1.0")
  (doc "glibc and systemd, no console login, read-only root, nothing to build with")

  (requires
    (buildroot "2025.02.16"))

  (external "br2-external")

  (provides
    (profile locked)))
